AFAIK: *THE* cursed magic marker trick involves writing then reading a
whole bunch of cursed scrolls of genocide while on a non-diggable
non-graveyard no teleport level (specifically, Sokoban) to reverse
genocide Wraiths, (i.e. "Summon Yummies!").  There are some other
things worth reverse-genociding under specific circumstances.  For
example:

foo-giants: Wimpy and you have a tinning kit
foo-dragons: resistances and scales, (wand of undead turning and
tinning kit helpful here)
(master) mind flayers:  Brain food, lots of caution is advised.


As for destroy armour, it takes fewer marker charges to write than
enchant armour, and is therefore a better way to foo-proof undamaged
armour.

Some other productive uses of cursed scrolls
1) cursed non-confused create monster:  Altar-camping without the
spell.
2) cursed (or confused) food detection:  Locates potions, probably
never worth writing.
3) cursed punishment:  Makes your heavy iron ball *very* heavy,
sometimes useful.

